{
  "$comment": "VAPP-119 the `exp:` binding SOURCES ×4 beyond devices (web-pinned per platform) and records (app-records.json): what an app host emits for `exp:issues`, `exp:boards`, `exp:members`, `exp:sessions`, `exp:comments` and `exp:attachments` over the team's synced rows, the SAME on web (TanStack DB), desktop (the store), iOS (GRDB) and Android (Room): the TS reference `app-sources.ts` (`sourceValue(name, params, store, {me})`); desktop `domain::app_sources`, iOS `AppSources.swift`, Android `AppSources.kt` replay every case of `cases` over `store` (one team's rows, ISO timestamps). QUERY (params as `parseSource` gives them): `limit` (`limits.default`, capped at `limits.max`); issues: `board=<id|slug>` (unknown = empty), `status=<anchor>`, `priority=<p>`, `assignee=<userId|me|none>`, `search=<text>` (case-insensitive substring of title or identifier), `sort=sortOrder|updatedAt|createdAt` (sortOrder asc by default, the timestamps desc), `order=asc|desc`; sessions: `status=`, `mine=1`; comments / attachments: `issue=<identifier|id>` (REQUIRED: without a resolvable issue the value is null). VALUES: issues {rows: [{id, identifier, title, status, priority, assignee, assigneeName, board, boardSlug, dueDate, updatedAt, value: identifier, label: `identifier title`}], count}; boards {rows: [{id, slug, name, prefix, icon, color, value: id, label: name}] (live boards by sortOrder, then name), count}; members {rows: [{id, name, email, avatar, role, value: id, label: name}] (by name), count, me}; the `value` + `label` pair makes a row a Select / ChipInput option (`shape: option`), so an app binds the rows straight into `options` / `suggestions`; sessions {rows: [{id, title, status, busy, needsInput, kind: thread|agent, updatedAt}] (roots only, no app editor sessions, newest first), count}; comments {rows: [{id, body, author, authorName, parent, source, createdAt}] (oldest first), count}; attachments {rows: [{id, name, type, size, url: /api/attachments/<id> (the media policy resolves it), width, height, uploader, uploaderName, createdAt}] (oldest first), count}. `count` counts before the limit; ties sort by id; text compares by code points (no locale). A name outside `sources` emits null.",
